.SH "DECODER PIXEL ASPECT"
libsixel uses the first raster attribute command
.B "\[dq] Pan ; Pad ; Ph ; Pv"
before SIXEL data to determine pixel aspect (vertical:horizontal).
A missing or zero Pan or Pad selects 1:1 aspect.
When Pan/Pad is an integer greater than one, each decoded row is repeated
that many times; other ratios retain one output row per SIXEL pixel.
Horizontal dimensions are unchanged. DCS macro P1 and grid size P3 do not
change decoded pixel aspect. Later raster commands can update Ph/Pv but
cannot change the aspect after the first raster command or SIXEL data.
.PP
Ph and Pv specify output pixels. A partial final group of repeated rows
ends exactly at Pv when the data fits the declared raster. Existing trusted
raster clipping and image size limits still apply; excessive scaled heights
are errors. In sequence and animation decoding, each image is expanded
before its painted pixels are composed onto the retained output canvas.

